# Suda Design Licensing & Distribution Architecture

**Document Status:** DRAFT — PENDING TECHNICAL & LEGAL VERIFICATION  
**Product:** Suda Design (Android Edition)  
**Last Updated:** 2026-11-01  

---

## 1. Underlying Open-Source Engine (PhotoCraft)

The underlying codebase of this application incorporates and derives from the **PhotoCraft** image editor engine, developed by the ArtCraft Team and open-source contributors:

- **Upstream Repository:** https://github.com/storytold/photocraft
- **Upstream Licenses:** Dual-licensed under the **Apache License, Version 2.0** (`LICENSE-APACHE`) or the **MIT License** (`LICENSE-MIT`), at the user's election.
- **Upstream Copyright:** (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and PhotoCraft contributors.

Nothing in this document or in the distribution of Suda Design modifies, restricts, supersedes, or limits any rights, freedoms, or permissions granted to recipients under the original MIT or Apache-2.0 licenses with respect to upstream PhotoCraft source code.

---

## 2. Proprietary Brand Assets & Trademarks (Separated from Software Copyright)

In accordance with Section 6 of the Apache License, Version 2.0 (which explicitly states that trademark rights are not granted), the following brand and visual identity elements are **NOT** licensed under MIT or Apache-2.0:

1. **Brand Marks & Trade Names:** "Suda Design", "Sd", "SudaDesign", and associated logos.
2. **Proprietary Graphical Identity:** The stylized multi-chromatic color-splash "Sd" vector art, splash screens, custom app launcher icons (`ic_launcher`), and trade dress.
3. **Commercial Identity:** Marketing materials, store descriptions, and distinctive visual presentation.

**Ownership Status:** All rights, title, and interest in and to these trademarks and proprietary visual assets are reserved exclusively by **`INDIVIDUAL_OWNER`** under applicable trademark and copyright laws. They are not assigned to any corporate vehicle until formal incorporation of a company and execution of a written assignment agreement.

Downstream distributors modifying the open-source code are reminded to comply with trademark law and remove proprietary trademarks, logos, and commercial branding to avoid consumer confusion.

---

## 3. Original Modifications & Contributions

- **Scope:** Custom Android GameActivity integrations, JNI bridges, low-latency soft keyboard (IME) input pipelines, mobile responsive layout dialog adaptors, and build packaging configurations.
- **Authorship:** Authored by `INDIVIDUAL_OWNER`.
- **Status:** Unverified in formal copyright registries; subject to proof of authorship and clean-room provenance.
- **Licensing:** Provided in this repository alongside upstream components under permissive open-source terms, reserving trademark rights.

---

## 4. Official Compiled Binary Distribution

Official compiled application binaries distributed via the Google Play Store or authorized channels are provided as free software for personal and commercial creative use, subject to the **End User License Agreement (EULA)** located at `legal/users/EULA.md`. 

The EULA governs the compiled binary artifact and user output ownership, without restricting the underlying open-source source code rights.

